# openssh-client.sed-patch  (applied to ssh_config)
#
# Enable the OQS post-quantum host-key + public-key signature algorithms in the
# client config by default, so `qp-ssh host` connects to a PQ qp-sshd with no
# -o overrides. '+' augments the built-in algorithm lists rather than replacing
# them, so classic SSH (ECDSA/Ed25519/RSA) still works. (mlkem1024 KEX is already
# offered by default in the OQS client, so only the signature lists need this.)
$a\
\
# qp-ssh: post-quantum defaults ('+' augments the classic algorithms)\
Host *\
HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-mldsa-87,ssh-falcon1024\
PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms +ssh-mldsa-87,ssh-falcon1024
